          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dictō, dictāre — \"to say repeatedly; to dictate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Magister versūs discipulīs dictābat. The teacher used to dictate verses to the pupils."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dictō, dictāre, dictāvī, dictātum, built on dīcō: to say over and over, for someone to take down. English dictate."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dictō is built on dīcō \"to say\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), with the ending -tō of a repeated act. English dictate comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
