              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pēnsum, pēnsī — \"a task, a day's work\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ancillae pēnsum suum perfēcērunt. The maids finished their day's work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pēnsum, pēnsī n., the participle of pendō, to weigh: the wool weighed out to a spinner each day, then any set task."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pēnsum is the participle of pendō \"to weigh out\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): the wool weighed out for a day's spinning."
            }
          ]
        },
